# This repository is PUBLIC (github.com/Kvalnir/ast, served at
# kvalnir.github.io/ast/). Everything matched here is kept out of it.
#
# Scope, honestly: .gitignore is hygiene, not enforcement. It only stops
# *untracked* files from being swept up by `git add -A`. It does nothing about
# text pasted into a file that is already tracked, and `git add -f` overrides
# it outright. Treat it as the floor, not the guarantee.
#
# Note for later: tools/*.json are generated by tools/*.py but are deliberately
# tracked. Do not add a blanket `*.json` rule.


# ── Secrets & credentials ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
.netrc
.npmrc
.htpasswd
credentials.json
secrets.json
/secrets/


# ── Personal data & PII ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Loose media at the repo root, which in practice means screenshots. A capture
# of a real browser window leaks more than the page: tabs, bookmarks, profile
# name, notifications, the OS user in the title bar. Anchored with a leading
# slash so genuine site art under assets/ stays committable.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.gif
/*.webp
/*.bmp
/*.mp4
/*.mov
/*.webm
/screenshots/
/recordings/

# Personal working files — drafts, scratch, anything not meant to be read by
# strangers. Keep private thinking in here and it can never be committed.
/private/
/scratch/
/notes/
*.local
*.local.md
*.local.json

# Data drops. Nothing this site needs arrives as a spreadsheet or a database,
# so if one appears it is either an export or a dump — both plausible PII.
*.csv
*.tsv
*.xlsx
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.bak
*.dump
*.har

# Logs can carry paths, hostnames, and IPs.
*.log


# ── Python (tools/ — generators, not part of the served site) ───────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.python-version


# ── OS & editor ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
# Windows mark-of-the-web alternate-data-stream sidecars, created under WSL
*:Zone.Identifier
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~


# ── Stray dev-environment dotfiles ──────────────────────────────────────────
# These show up untracked in this repo's root but are shell/editor config, not
# project files. Under WSL several are character-special files rather than
# directories, so they need bare patterns as well as the dir-only ones above.
# .gitmodules is listed for that reason too — if this repo ever gains a real
# submodule, remove that line, because the real file must be committed.
.idea
.vscode
.bash_profile
.bashrc
.gitconfig
.gitmodules
.profile
.ripgreprc
.zprofile
.zshrc
.mcp.json
.claude/
